{% comment %}
A data-driven campaign: the shape is fixed, the content comes from the database. This is the
case the whole MJML-through-Django-templates arrangement exists for — nobody retypes a date,
and the artwork grid is however many pieces are actually in the show.

Copy this file to make a new recurring format. Set Campaign.template_name to the filename
and pass the objects it needs; see gallery/campaigns.py::render_campaign.

A template can also place the author's own Markdown body inside its layout, which is what the
optional note below does — so a recurring format does not have to mean identical wording every
time, and adding a sentence to one mailing is not a deploy. Two forms are available:

  {{ campaign_body }}          a whole <mj-section>, to drop between sections (used here)
  {{ campaign_body_blocks }}   just the contents, to drop inside an existing <mj-column>

Using the wrong one nests an mj-section inside an mj-column, which MJML rejects with an error
that does not mention either.
{% endcomment %}
<mj-section padding="8px 24px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text font-size="26px" font-weight="bold" padding="12px 0 4px">{{ show.name }}</mj-text>
    <mj-text color="#666666" padding="0 0 12px">
      {{ show.start|date:"j F" }}–{{ show.end|date:"j F Y" }}{% if site %} · {{ site.name }}{% endif %}
    </mj-text>
    {% if show.description %}<mj-text padding="8px 0">{{ show.description|striptags|truncatewords:60 }}</mj-text>{% endif %}
    <mj-button href="{{ show_url }}" background-color="#198754" color="#ffffff" padding="16px 0">
      See the show
    </mj-button>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

{% comment %}
Whatever the curator wrote for this particular announcement, if anything. Between the header
and the artwork grid, so a note reads as an introduction to the works rather than a postscript.
{% endcomment %}
{% if campaign.body_markdown.strip %}{{ campaign_body }}{% endif %}

{% if artworks %}
<mj-section padding="0 24px">
  {% for artwork in artworks|slice:":3" %}
  <mj-column width="33%">
    {% if artwork.card_md %}<mj-image src="{{ artwork.card_md.url }}" alt="{{ artwork.name }}" padding="4px" />{% endif %}
    <mj-text font-size="13px" align="center" padding="4px">
      {{ artwork.name }}{% if artwork.artists.all %}<br /><span style="color:#888888">{{ artwork.artists.all.0.name }}</span>{% endif %}
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
  {% endfor %}
</mj-section>
{% endif %}
